If you've seen treasure hunters, you might think that a treasure map has been drawn on the back of the Declaration of Independence.
However, this is not true. Although something is written on the back of the document, it is not a treasure map.
On the back of the Declaration of Independence are the words “Original of the Declaration of Independence of 4 July 1776”. The text is on the underside of the document, written upside down.
Although the author is certainly not known, it is clear that a large parchment document (dimensions of 293⁄4 x 241⁄2 inches) was curled into a role and stored not long after its creation.
It is therefore likely that the entry was added simply as a sticker.
