Tibetan Buddhism is based on Buddha's teachings, but has been extended by the Mahayan path of love and many techniques from Indian yoga.
The principles of Tibetan Buddhism are, in principle, very simple. They are kundalini yoga, meditation, and a journey of all-encompassing love.
In Kundalini yoga, the energy of Kundalini (enlightenment energy) is awakened by the positions of this yoga, breathing exercises, mantras and visualizations.
The centerpiece of Tibetan meditation is Deity Yoga. Through the visualization of different deities, energy channels are cleared, chakras are activated, and an enlightened consciousness was created.
